<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Events that can happen together</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(s=6)"]]<p>Two fair dice are rolled.</p>[[else]]<p>A fair die is rolled and a fair spinner with \({@s@}\) equal sectors numbered 1 to \({@s@}\) is spun.</p>[[/if]]<p>A is the event <q>the [[if test="is(s=6)"]]first die[[else]]die[[/if]] shows [[if test="is(nA=1)"]]a 6[[else]]a 5 or a 6[[/if]]</q>. B is the event <q>the [[if test="is(s=6)"]]second die[[else]]spinner[[/if]] shows [[if test="is(nB=1)"]]\({@s@}\)[[else]]1 or 2[[/if]]</q>.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) Find \(P(\text{A and B})\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \(P(\text{neither A nor B})\).</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find \(P(\text{A or B, or both})\).</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(P(\text{A}) = \dfrac{{@nA@}}{6}\) and \(P(\text{B}) = \dfrac{{@nB@}}{{@s@}}\). The [[if test="is(s=6)"]]first die[[else]]die[[/if]] and the [[if test="is(s=6)"]]second die[[else]]spinner[[/if]] are independent. There are \(6 \times {@s@} = {@n@}\) equally likely outcomes.</p><p>(a) \(P(\text{A and B}) = \dfrac{{@nA@}}{6} \times \dfrac{{@nB@}}{{@s@}} = {@ta1@}\): \({@nA*nB@}\) of the \({@n@}\) outcomes.</p><p>(b) \(P(\text{neither}) = \dfrac{{@6-nA@}}{6} \times \dfrac{{@s-nB@}}{{@s@}} = {@ta2@}\).</p><p>(c) A and B can happen together, so do not just add. \(P(\text{A or B, or both}) = 1 - P(\text{neither}) = 1 - {@ta2@} = {@ta3@}\). Check by counting: A has \({@nA*s@}\) outcomes and B has \({@6*nB@}\), and the \({@nA*nB@}\) where both happen are in both lists, so \({@nA*s@} + {@6*nB@} - {@nA*nB@} = {@nA*s+6*nB-nA*nB@}\) of the \({@n@}\) outcomes.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: [s, nA, nB]: A = die shows 6 (nA 1) or 5 or 6 (nA 2); B = spinner (or second die) shows s (nB 1) or 1 or 2 (nB 2). Source: original. */
L: [[4,1,1],[5,1,1],[8,1,2],[10,2,1],[4,1,2],[5,2,2],[8,1,1],[10,1,2],[6,2,2],[6,1,2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
s: L[ix][1]; nA: L[ix][2]; nB: L[ix][3];
n: 6*s;
ta1: nA*nB/n; ta2: (6-nA)*(s-nB)/n; ta3: 1-ta2;
tl1: min(1/200,ta1/20); tl2: min(1/200,ta2/20); tl3: min(1/200,ta3/20);
/* diagnostics */
add1: nA/6+nB/s;
notboth2: 1-ta1;
dbl3: nA/6+nB/s;
both3: ta1;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
